# "A land you control" is the ability's controller's (CR 113.8, 602.2a): the enchanted land has the ability, so its
# controller activates it, whoever controls Equinox. Bot2 casts Equinox on Bot1's Plains, then aims Stone Rain at that
# Plains; Bot1 taps it, and Stone Rain would destroy a land Bot1 controls, so it is countered - though it would destroy no
# land of Bot2's, Equinox's controller.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Equinox
Stone Rain
Mountain x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Equinox.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Plains)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Stone Rain.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Plains)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate(Stack.Stone Rain; Ability: Counter)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield = Equinox; Mox Pearl
Bot2.Graveyard = Stone Rain; Black Lotus
